# Kalpitiya 60 MW — Envision EN-206 wind proposal and turbine performance document, 7 September 2026
#
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# HANDLING NOTE — KALPITIYA60MW-WIND-HANDLING-2026-09-21
#
# This block is the ONLY statement of how this package is handled. The corpus README, the
# source_packages README and the deduplication receipt cite the identifier above rather than
# restating the reasoning, the authority or the route. One copy cannot drift. Five copies of
# the equivalent statement for the NSO offers package disagreed with one another on 4 September
# 2026, and that disagreement was a blocking finding of the RECRUIT-01 review of that change.
# `tests/lint/test_nso_corpus_manifest_integrity.py` fails loudly if a second copy appears or if
# a citation goes stale.
#
# 1. THE DOCUMENTS ARE PRIVATE.
#    The two source documents, their extracts, the derived data, the registers and the two
#    evaluations are held in the PRIVATE repository arunakulat/DutchBay_RAG at
#    corpus/kalpitiya_60mw_2026_envision_wind/, merged to that repository's main at commit
#    28204a5 (PR #6). No document in this package, and no extract of one, has ever been
#    committed to this public repository. The 16 hashes below are the whole of what this
#    repository holds about the package.
#
# 2. WHY THE ROUTE WAS SELECTED.
#    Both documents are restricted, on two different grounds.
#
#    The turbine performance document is a Released controlled document, PMD-004447 Rev A,
#    7 September 2026, and is marked Confidential in the document-control header of every page.
#    The proposal and energy yield study carries an express bar on reproduction without the
#    written permission of its copyright holder. It carries no document number and no revision
#    of its own, so it can be cited only by hash — which is what this manifest is for.
#
#    No written authorization instrument is held for either document. Neither
#    PUBLICATION_AUTHORIZATION.md, which enumerates four files from the 6 August 2026 tranche,
#    nor the 29 August reversal, which turned on material forming part of the bid submitted to
#    NSO, reaches OEM turbine performance data or an unsolicited commercial proposal. This
#    repository is public, and a push to it is effectively irreversible: the content can be
#    cloned, cached and indexed before any later removal takes effect.
#
#    Route selected on the precedent already set twice in this corpus — the 21 August checklist
#    dossier and the 3 September commercial offers, both held outside this repository and
#    recorded here by manifest. See NSO250MW-OFFERS-HANDLING-2026-09-04 for the reasoning in
#    the offers case; it is cited, not restated.
#
# 3. THIS FILE IS MANIFEST-ONLY, AND WHAT THAT STILL DISCLOSES.
#    Unlike the offers manifest, this file recites no figure from either document: no power
#    curve value, no thrust coefficient, no energy yield, no wind speed, no loss factor, no
#    coordinate, no price. The evaluation of the package and the comparison against the Dutch
#    Bay Final EIA and feasibility study are held privately at the paths recorded below, and
#    their findings are not reproduced here.
#
#    What the filenames themselves carry is disclosed rather than glossed over. They name the
#    turbine model and its de-rate, the controlled-document number and revision, the site and
#    its nominal capacity, and — in the air density embedded in one derived filename — one
#    modelling parameter. The deduplication receipt beside this file reproduces the AS-SUPPLIED
#    filenames of the two source documents, which carry two further parameters: the unit count
#    and the hub height. A manifest cannot identify an object without naming it and a receipt
#    cannot be checked without naming what arrived, so this is the irreducible minimum, and it
#    is recorded as a disclosure rather than treated as none.
#
# 4. NOTHING HERE HAS BEEN PROMOTED.
#    No figure from this package has entered a scenario, a model input, a baseline or a report.
#    The evaluation holds two open questions that must be answered in writing by the issuer
#    before anything in the package is used: which power curve produced the energy yield
#    appendix, and what the wind data provenance and uncertainty basis are. Recording a package
#    is not accepting it.
